nodecode-postel is a rewrite of robinfaraj's robinfaraj/postel-mcp:

https://github.com/robinfaraj/postel-mcp
commit adaa9363ffbaf6b74a5a11e15f88acb0392d6406
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 JRS Content Solutions UG (haftungsbeschränkt) (LICENSE)

The original was a portable manifest - plugin.json, mcp.json and one Markdown
skill - that pointed the harness at Postel's hosted MCP server and taught the
model the order of work. The rewrite keeps what a user gets: research on what
went viral, drafts in the user's own voice, threads and media, a LinkedIn first
comment, listing and reading the workspace's posts, scheduling and publishing,
and the account's plan and connected networks. Those became eight tools in
Common Lisp that call Postel's own REST API (documented in the same repository)
with an API key from the cell's section, and the skill's writing advice became
the manual topic `:postel` plus each tool's description. Left out: the MCP
transport and its OAuth sign-in, because the keyed REST API reaches the same
operations and a cell can hold a key; the marketing and per-client install
sections of the README, which are about other harnesses; and the tools the REST
API does not name (updating and deleting a draft, attaching media to an existing
draft, the brand and voice-profile listings), so the rewrite speaks only for the
endpoints the original repository documents.
